{{also|Equus}}
==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* [[equos]] ''(till the middle of the first century B.C.)''
* [[ecus]] ''(the regular development, later remodeled to ''equus'' on the analogy of the stem ''equ-'' as remained, e.g., in the genitive'' equi.)

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|itc-pro|la}} {{term/t|itc-pro|*ekwos}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₁éḱwos||horse}}. Cognates include Ancient  Greek {{term|ἵππος|tr=hippos|sc=polytonic|lang=grc}}, Sanskrit {{term|अश्व|tr=áśva|sc=Deva|lang=sa}} and Old Armenian {{term|էշ||donkey|tr=ēš|lang=xcl}}, Tocharian B {{term|yakwe|lang=txb}}, Gaulish {{term|epos|lang=cel-gau}}.

